==Finnish==

===Etymology===
From {{inh|fi|urj-fin-pro|*südän}}, from {{inh|fi|urj-pro|*śüdäme}}. Cognate with {{cog|et|süda}}, {{cog|myv|седей}}, {{cog|mns-nor|сым}} and {{cog|hu|szív|id=heart}}.

===Pronunciation===
{{fi-p|syDän}}
* Note that the pronunciation of inflected or derived words with the stem {{m|fi||sydäm-}} is somewhat irregular, as the ''m'' is often pronounced long, as if {{m|fi||sydämm-}}.

===Noun===
{{fi-noun}}

# [[heart]] {{gl|organ}}
# {{lb|fi|figurative}} [[heart]] {{gl|one's feelings and emotions; seat of the affections or sensibilities}}
# [[heart]] {{gl|symbol representing a heart, except on playing cards}}
#: {{syn|fi|hertta|t1=heart symbol|qq1=including on playing cards}}
# [[heart]], [[core]] {{gl|centre, essence, most important thing}}
#: {{syn|fi|ydin}}
#: {{coi|fi|reaktori'''sydän'''|(nuclear) reactor '''core'''}}
# [[wick]] {{gl|of a candle}}

